cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its results in published work, please cite the
  relevant version below AND the underlying physics references listed at
  the bottom. See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md for the full list of observational
  data sources used and how to cite them. v0.3-prelim+T71.7 (T71.7
  KiSS-SIDM timeout closure 2026-08-28: T38a N=5e4 dwarf re-run with
  KISS_SIDM_TIMEOUT_S=7200 hit 2/10 snapshots in 7200s — UFD KiSS-SIDM
  declared structurally out-of-session; wrapper-level timeout env var
  shipped (commit cdb9028); Brower N_f=8 lattice deferred per
  reviewer Assessment.docx ¶52 (wrong N_f + undocumented columns +
  conformal-window risk). T71.5 Tier B closure 2026-08-28: Drobczyk
  quantitative χ² test added (t68b, χ²=213.62, strong tension vs
  arXiv:2506.22997); LZ WS2024 stale-claim correction (already in
  production since R12 via t30_lz_real_posterior.loglike_lz_real, HEPData
  155182, 26 mass points); KiSS-SIDM UFD fidelity deferred with rationale
  (canonical halo converged at N=1e4-1e5). V0_6_ROADMAP: 9 of 15 items
  shipped across T71.2 → T71.7. Earlier closed rounds: T71.4 (3 v0.6
  items in parallel: hier-sparc +0.10 log Z, bullet_sens +1.74 log Z,
  CHANNEL_STATUS dict); T71.3 (R7 closure: nlive=2000 (Nc,Nf) scan via
  7-way parallel background runner, scan converged); T71.2 (R16 closure:
  ksfr_mask_max_at_runtime field + config_hash field, 575/0/6 tests);
  T71.1 (R15 closure: inelastic + nlive=2000 + KSFR mask extension
  confound found) and the H3+H4 sensitivity report at
  v0.3-prelim/docs/H3_H4_SENSITIVITY_REPORT.md are the most recent
  closed rounds at the time of the most recent public release. T71.8
  doc-only audit upgrade (2026-08-28): (2,2) KSFR ESTIMATED → LATTICE
  after re-reading Arthur 1602.06559 via Bennett Sp(4) Fig 17 (count
  shifts 2/2/3 → 3/2/2); Sp(4) explicitly distinguished from SU(2).
  T71.8.1 (2026-08-29): lifted KiSS-SIDM UFD timeout verdict into
  standing docs — KISS_SIDM_CANONICAL_N, KISS_SIDM_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S in
  config.py; KiSS-SIDM Quick Start section in README; "⚠️ Known caveats"
  block at top of FINDINGS.md. No version bump (doc-only).
